  "elements": [
    {
      "id": "aNh2wc_Qi9ptZUlDnGhbv",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -28.730490848144996,
      "y": 184.75338931205556,
      "width": 842.8733069161483,
      "height": 1452.7882807635715,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "a0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1354326884,
      "version": 3831,
      "versionNonce": 1261559772,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1780812979710,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "look at first preorder to get root\nfind it in inorder to get the left and right sections\nleft section size = idx, right section size = inorder.size()\n- idx - 1 = 3\nleft section [0:0]:\n   get root from next element in preorder\n   you only need to read 1 element since idx = 1. so stop\nthere; left side done\nright section [2:4]:\n    find root by checking next preorder elem\n    find it in inorder. new root = 20. repeat process for\narray [2:4]\nso actually for left section as well youd 'repeat process'\nfor [0:0]\n\nwe should work in pointers right\nwe have a single pointer for preorder to find the next\nroot, and two at inorder to define the bounds of the\nsearch kinda thing. and u also need the one for the\ninorder index of your current inorder\nlets call them... i r l mid\ni guess theyd be global class members wouldnt they\ni wonder if theres recursion involved here...\n\nfunction(root, l, r):\n    if (l <= r + 1):\n        return\n \n    mid = inorder.find(*l, *r, preorder[i])\n    i++\n    root->left = new node(preorder[i])\n    function(root->left, l, mid)\n    i++\n    root->right = new node(preorder[i])\n    function(root->right, mid + 1, len + 1)\n\n\n        \n",
      "fontSize": 29.800785246432238,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "look at first preorder to get root\nfind it in inorder to get the left and right sections\nleft section size = idx, right section size = inorder.size() - idx - 1 = 3\nleft section [0:0]:\n   get root from next element in preorder\n   you only need to read 1 element since idx = 1. so stop there; left side done\nright section [2:4]:\n    find root by checking next preorder elem\n    find it in inorder. new root = 20. repeat process for array [2:4]\nso actually for left section as well youd 'repeat process' for [0:0]\n\nwe should work in pointers right\nwe have a single pointer for preorder to find the next root, and two at inorder to define the bounds of the search kinda thing. and u also need the one for the inorder index of your current inorder\nlets call them... i r l mid\ni guess theyd be global class members wouldnt they\ni wonder if theres recursion involved here...\n\nfunction(root, l, r):\n    if (l <= r + 1):\n        return\n \n    mid = inorder.find(*l, *r, preorder[i])\n    i++\n    root->left = new node(preorder[i])\n    function(root->left, l, mid)\n    i++\n    root->right = new node(preorder[i])\n    function(root->right, mid + 1, len + 1)\n\n\n        \n",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
